                <pb facs="0626" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7512: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macgowan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-20T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 53, October 12, 4 p.m. Refrain from requesting Japanese protection, either
                    jointly with the other members of the Consular Corps or singly as American
                    Consul.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
